task:
Alert: Account management alert: a new account named support_tmp was created around 13:42 UTC on 2026-11-10. Review activity between 13:20 and 14:20 UTC and decide whether it is malicious.

Environment context (from the organization's asset and service inventory):
Organization: Lakeview Accounting (domain LAKEVIEW-ACCT / lakeview-acct.local), a small accounting office.
Hosts: workstations WS-DWELLS-01 (dana.wells, accountant), WS-RIYER-01 (raj.iyer, analyst), WS-KORTEGA-01 (kim.ortega, IT administrator), WS-TNGUYEN-01 (tara.nguyen, help desk); servers DC-LV-01 (domain controller, DNS), FILE-LV-01 (file server, finance shares, scheduled jobs), PROXY-LV-01 (explicit web proxy, port 8080; all web egress goes through it). There is no VPN; remote administration is only done from WS-KORTEGA-01 inside the office.
Accounts: kim.ortega is the only IT administrator. tara.nguyen (help desk) can create domain accounts but is not an administrator. Service accounts: svc-backup (Vaultline backup agent on FILE-LV-01) and svc-reporting (ReportSync job on FILE-LV-01, runs every minute and re-authenticates on each run).
Change calendar for 2026-11-10: the svc-reporting password is scheduled to be rotated by IT at 13:30 UTC (CHG-2291); the ReportSync job on FILE-LV-01 must then be updated manually with the new password. Monthly workstation patching by IT is scheduled during business hours.
IT practices: kim.ortega patches workstations by remotely running \\FILE-LV-01\IT\scripts\Install-MonthlyPatches.ps1 with PowerShell from WS-KORTEGA-01. The help desk creates temporary contractor accounts on request, always named temp.<name>, added only to the Contractors domain group; temporary accounts never receive administrator rights. No other account creation is expected.
Approved software and services: Microsoft 365 / OneDrive; Vaultline (vaultline-backup.com) offsite backup; DataGrid Analytics desktop (installed in C:\Program Files\DataGrid\Analytics\ on analyst workstations), whose updater dgupdate.exe checks update.datagrid-analytics.com over HTTPS about every 5 minutes. No other file-sharing, cloud-storage or remote-access services are approved.

Objective: Determine whether the available security evidence supports a malicious-activity finding, a benign disposition, or an insufficient-evidence determination.

Evidence is available only through these tools: list_sources, query, get_record. Retrieve evidence with the tools before answering. You may make at most 30 tool calls.

